 "inference": [
  "Registry DisabledDamageThreshold and ClearDisabledDamageThreshold are the same number on every vehicle, so with the registry default in use (the pattern of L3327 and L3339) there is one threshold and the order question of L3347 does not matter: tanks 400 of 1200, the UH60 500 of 1500, every other vehicle 300.",
  "That is one third of health for tanks and the UH60, 30 percent for 1000-health vehicles, 37.5 percent for the JLTV and Marauder (the AH6M has no registry row; its own fields hold 300 of 700).",
  "The own Field_1a7c18f1 holds a lower number (200 on most vehicles) than its registry row on 19 vehicles: one more own-versus-registry dispute. Which registry row belongs to that field is still not stored.",
  "This corrects the reading offered in L3347 (critical below 200, recover above 400 for a tank): by the registry rows a tank is critical below 400.",
  "That the 'disabled' state is EA's 'critical health' remains a join by meaning."
 ],
 "unresolved": [
  "Whether the registry default (400) or the own value (200) is the entry point on a tank. Test: damage a tank in steps; the critical warning and slowed regeneration start at 400 or at 200.",
  "RepairRateModifier 1.0 on every vehicle: what repair rate it scales was not read here."
 ],
